  "query_preview": "..Today and Sunday...A cut-off low is currently spinning\nover southern california this morning. This low is expected to \ngradually meander it's way eastward over the weekend, keeping \ncooler temperatures in store through Sunday. Precipitation chances\nalso look to creep back into northern Arizona with some residual \nmoisture still place. The best chances look to be mainly along and\nnorth of the Mogollon Rim today, with some isolated activity \nlingering across the Four Corners region on Sunday. While a few \nbrief heavy downpours could be possible, much of the rainfall \nlooks to be light. Thus, the threat for additional flash flooding \nlooks to be minimal but the rain will certainly add to the already\nelevated area waterways.\n\nMonday through Friday...As the closed-low lifts into Colorado, weak \nridging, or even quasi-zonal flow looks to build into the southwest. \nGradually warming temperatures and dry conditions look to prevail \ninto much of next week. A deepening trough over the Pacific \nNorthwest looks to potentially breakdown this pattern near the end \nof next week, however model guidance remains uncertain in the exact \ntrack of the low. Nevertheless, cooler temperatures and potentially \na return of precipitation looks possible near the end of the week.",
